            <ArticleTitle>A chiral smectic structure assembled from nanosheets and nanorods.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1868-1871</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc08337d</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Here we report a novel chiral smectic through self-assembling two-dimensional graphene oxide nanosheets and one-dimensional cellulose nanorods. As shown by a phase diagram, the formation of the chiral smectic strictly depends on the ratio of nanosheets to nanorods as well as the concentration of the composite colloid. It would open up a new way for the development of mesoscopic materials with tunable physical properties, such as optical metamaterials with application in optical modulation and mechanochromic sensors.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
